# Per-producer path scopes.
#
# The bundle names its concepts by the producer of the thing they
# describe (usgs-, nwis-, nldi- for the water agency; imerg-, nldas2-
# and gesdisc- for that data centre; mod16- for the land processes one;
# swot- and hydrocron- for the ocean one; openet- and snodas- for the
# rest). Those prefixes are what make single-producer stewardship
# possible: a steward at one agency can own the rules about their own
# products without owning anyone else's, and derive_credit reads each
# scope and lists it beside the steward it maps to.
#
# Every scope below resolves to the interim owner today. That is the
# point of writing them now: the structure exists, so accepting a
# steward is a one-line change to a handle rather than a rearrangement
# of the bundle, and the scope a steward is being asked to take is
# visible before they are asked.

# The water agency: gauges, the peaks record, basin delineation and the
# hydrologic units.
/knowledge/**/usgs-*   @PaulMRamirez
/knowledge/**/nwis-*   @PaulMRamirez
/knowledge/**/nldi-*   @PaulMRamirez

# The precipitation and land-surface forcing data centre.
/knowledge/**/imerg-*    @PaulMRamirez
/knowledge/**/nldas2-*   @PaulMRamirez
/knowledge/**/gesdisc-*  @PaulMRamirez

# The land processes data centre: evapotranspiration.
/knowledge/**/mod16-*  @PaulMRamirez

# The ocean data centre: the surface water mission and its time series
# service. Note that the mission's own product concepts live in the
# provider bundle and are owned there; what this scope covers is this
# plugin's use of them.
/knowledge/**/swot-*       @PaulMRamirez
/knowledge/**/hydrocron-*  @PaulMRamirez

# The soil moisture mission.
/knowledge/**/smap-*  @PaulMRamirez

# The evapotranspiration service, the snow assimilation, and the
# reservoir survey tables.
/knowledge/**/openet-*       @PaulMRamirez
/knowledge/**/snodas-*       @PaulMRamirez
/knowledge/**/reclamation-*  @PaulMRamirez
